    "chunk_text": "w;s \u00fafYI\n\nwxl 2451$11 - 2025 wf.daia;= ui 26 jeks w`.yrejdod - 2025.08.26No. 2451/11 - TUESDAY, 26 AUGUST , 2025\n\nEXTRAORDINARY\n\nY%S ,xld m%cd;dka;%sl iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha .ei\u00dc m;%h\n\nThe Gazette of the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka\n\n(Published by Authority)PART I : SECTION (I) \u2014 GENERAL\n\nGovernment Notifications\n\n1A- PG 7235 - 324 (08/2025) This Gazette Extraordinary can be downloaded from www.documents.gov.lk\n\nL. D.-B. 5/2025SRI LANKA ELECTRICITY ACT, No. 36 OF 2024\n\nREGULATIONS made by the Minister of Energy under Section 50 of the Sri Lanka Electricity Act, No. 36 of 2024, read with Paragraphs (f) of subsection (3) of Section 18 of that Act.\n\nPunya Sri Kumara Jayakodi, Minister of Energy.\n\nColombo,26th August, 2025.Regulations\n\n1. These Regulations may be cited as the Sri Lanka Energy Electricity (Terms and Conditions of Voluntary Retirement Scheme) Regulations of 2025.\n\n2. These Regulations shall apply to every officer and servant (hereinafter referred to as the \u201cemployee\u201d) of the Ceylon Electricity Board who do not opt to be assigned to a successor company and be entitled to voluntary retirement under a voluntary retirement scheme (hereinafter referred to as the \u201cvoluntary retirement scheme\u201d) referred to in the provisions of Paragraph (f) of subsection (3) of Section 18 of the Sri Lanka Electricity Act, No.36 of 2024.\n\n3. Any employee who is entitled to voluntary retirement under regulation 2 may make an application substantially in the form specified in the form specified in the Schedule hereto.\n\nI fldgi ( ^I& fPoh - YS% ,xld m%cd;dka;s%l iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha w;s \u00fafYI .ei\u00dc m;%h - 2025'08'26Part I : Sec. (I) - GAZETTE EXTRAORDINARY OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA - 26.08.20252A\n\n4. (1) The compensation payable under the voluntary retirement scheme, to the following categories of employees who are serving under the permanent cader of the Ceylon Electricity Board shall be as follows :-"
