    "chunk_size_bytes": 1923,
    "chunk_text": "8B. The driver of a motor vehicle shall not enter into or drive or use such motor vehicle on an expressway unless such motor vehicle is fitted with individual safety seat belts as specified in regulation 8E which function properly, to be worn by the driver, every passenger and individual occupying a seat and travelling therein.\n\n8D. (1) The application of the provisions of regulations 8A, 8B and 8C in respect of the following classes of motor vehicles shall commence after completion of three months from the date of coming into operation of regulations 8A, 8B and 8C:-\n\n(a) the driver or owner of a motor car driven or used on or entered into an expressway which has not been fitted by the manufacturer with an individual safety seat belt as specified in regulation 8E for the rear centre seat at the time of coming into operation of regulations 8A, 8B and 8C;\n\n(b) the driver or owner of a light motor coach, motor coach, heavy motor coach, dual-purpose vehicle, light motor lorry, heavy motor lorry or motor home vehicle driven or used on or entered into an expressway which has not been fitted by the manufacturer with individual safety seat belts as specified in regulation 8E for the rear centre seats or several rear seats at the time of coming into operation of regulations 8A. 8B and 8C;\n\n(c) the driver or owner of a dual-purpose vehicle, light motor coach, motor coach or heavy motor coach engaged in daily office transport service or school transport service and driven or used on or entered into an expressway which has not been fitted by the manufacturer with individual safety seats belt as specified in regulation 8E for the rear centre seats or several rear seats at the time of coming into operation of regulations 8 A, 8B and 8C.\n\n(2) The provisions of regulations 8A, 8B and 8C shall not apply to-\n\n(a) children under the age of twelve years and persons whose height does not exceed 135 centimeters;"
