    "chunk_text": "w;s \u00fafYI\n\nwxl 2456$34 - 2025 Tlaf;dan\u00be ui 01 jeks nodod - 2025.10'01No. 2456/34 - WEDNESDAY, OCTOBER 01, 2025\n\nEXTRAORDINARY\n\nY%S ,xld m%cd;dka;%sl iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha .ei\u00dc m;%h\n\nThe Gazette of the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka\n\n(Published by Authority)PART I : SECTION (I) \u2014 GENERAL\n\nGovernment Notifications\n\n1A - PG 45454 - 05 (10/2025) This Gazette Extraordinary can be downloaded from www.documents.gov.lk\n\nRULE MADE UNDER SECTION 45 (CHAPTER 190) OF THE POST OFFICE ORDINANCE\n\nMoney Orders issued with effect from 01.01.2022 to 31.12.2022\n\nA Money Order is valid for Six months from the last day of the month of its issue. Under exceptional circumstances, the payment of a lapsed Money Order is considered up to two years from the last day of the month of its issue. However, a Money Order cannot be revalidated or refunded after lapsing of two years from the last day of the months of its issue and the value of such Money Order is credited to Government Revenue.\n\n02. However, under the following exceptional circumstance, the value of a Money Order lapsed two years could be considered for refund from Government Revenue subject to the recovery of relevant charges.\n\nI. Money Order being produced in a court of law.\n\nII. The Money Order being retained in a Rent Control Board on legal Grounds.\n\nIII. Payee of the Money Order being out of the Country. (The passport should be produced.)\n\nIV. Payee being in a very bad state of health for a long period. (Should be supported by a Medical Certificate from a Government Medical Officer.)\n\n03. If the Money Orders, related to 2 (I) and (II) above, cannot be produced within three months from the date of publishing of this Gazette Notification, details of such Money Orders with the related case numbers etc., should be sent to the Controller of Money Order services in writing, If it is unable to produce Money Orders, It shall also be informed in writing."
